[{:db/id "q-115603/selection/4e8641b3cb277b07635b8e62ec1c6e93dad5212e3307ba76c4f4f45915fe36b6" :answer/id #uuid "648142c1-d79f-56b8-b114-b2f58a05afbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115603/selection/a4a7c18f96983532e4003d75c6450d6bba70b3da1af70c4c3421a446a2f66bd0" :answer/id #uuid "9b56cd30-d59a-5ebe-a8d9-0d2e47503704" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115603/selection/6db1b3e26b30525d4ed7a09400dccbe999a5c2e2b1954ea0dec60d75c907de2c" :answer/id #uuid "be1bd756-c4a5-5aa7-b698-0c8d6f814ed6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115603/selection/de0b677261bde629b5e156f8561b705314fbfb38516123f6ed9161ad8add8643" :answer/id #uuid "4ba1ce4b-8642-5253-981f-5f6bdf60b52a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115603/selection/3d2070a91b3f93e2ff3f01bbf9bffb1b6bac79b45237069ea1f5092d2b29dd3c" :answer/id #uuid "5711b977-9b22-548d-9138-4275415392b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115603/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "719be2f9-01a6-5d9c-9c2e-96801e89fd5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115603/selection/6db1b3e26b30525d4ed7a09400dccbe999a5c2e2b1954ea0dec60d75c907de2c" :answer-field/choices ["q-115603/selection/4e8641b3cb277b07635b8e62ec1c6e93dad5212e3307ba76c4f4f45915fe36b6" "q-115603/selection/a4a7c18f96983532e4003d75c6450d6bba70b3da1af70c4c3421a446a2f66bd0" "q-115603/selection/6db1b3e26b30525d4ed7a09400dccbe999a5c2e2b1954ea0dec60d75c907de2c" "q-115603/selection/de0b677261bde629b5e156f8561b705314fbfb38516123f6ed9161ad8add8643" "q-115603/selection/3d2070a91b3f93e2ff3f01bbf9bffb1b6bac79b45237069ea1f5092d2b29dd3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115603" :question/id #uuid "e2af71a7-077c-5a7d-81e7-d9c33fb34600" :question/math-academy-id "q-115603" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/assets/b472d30e6260b0e0f1ce4bc791c5ce3068d78a304711775e1327a4c3dbd8c3d3.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(2,-2).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(2,-2),$ we can substitute $x=2$ and $y=-2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-2)^{2} & =4p(2) \\\\ 4 & =8p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{2})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=\\frac{1}{2}$ is positive." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115603/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75fd35db-6b4e-5820-b6ac-925d24a0f117"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115603"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115601/selection/7e8e26b4e22cebd39c65c34d407e675ae4d095ece86c0632bef2c0ced5773fea" :answer/id #uuid "0492805e-b19e-5b17-b646-be1a70c747f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115601/selection/d3a0f4fff8cf2be9e994be6ef6f9d0493097211871081ec91b651d1d230dcc53" :answer/id #uuid "abc04700-174b-5d32-a7a4-d01666565b6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{9}{8}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115601/selection/2381990babb18cc615a66c62495f1fd7c6db6b5da4727049dc6dc0bd8583a5be" :answer/id #uuid "05285e91-6563-5d86-9ea1-5d8ab0c6b499" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115601/selection/77fd7412b99188f3283aff2cb4f196a3e34d18cc12692712c2a2a86e00952fee" :answer/id #uuid "abaa488b-002f-5654-98fc-b9fd91f0605d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115601/selection/5b14f578517c9a7f2004869f81a38ebf7e16b376232fb580bc0a2180fbb43187" :answer/id #uuid "e6064e2a-e921-5d2e-8256-3fcb18b99120" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{9}{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115601/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "75cb4592-93f7-5a63-8588-acebaddca7b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115601/selection/2381990babb18cc615a66c62495f1fd7c6db6b5da4727049dc6dc0bd8583a5be" :answer-field/choices ["q-115601/selection/7e8e26b4e22cebd39c65c34d407e675ae4d095ece86c0632bef2c0ced5773fea" "q-115601/selection/d3a0f4fff8cf2be9e994be6ef6f9d0493097211871081ec91b651d1d230dcc53" "q-115601/selection/2381990babb18cc615a66c62495f1fd7c6db6b5da4727049dc6dc0bd8583a5be" "q-115601/selection/77fd7412b99188f3283aff2cb4f196a3e34d18cc12692712c2a2a86e00952fee" "q-115601/selection/5b14f578517c9a7f2004869f81a38ebf7e16b376232fb580bc0a2180fbb43187"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115601" :question/id #uuid "d2494c4e-4dc3-5d72-87cc-1d73c73f8edf" :question/math-academy-id "q-115601" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/assets/4938d034c766b78e1da1a5bd19f2a12b314f772ca4819cd52d4f1463ff1ae3a4.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(3,2).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(3,2),$ we can substitute $x=3$ and $y=2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {2}^{2} & =4p(3) \\\\ 4 & =12p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{3})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=\\frac{1}{3}$ is positive." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115601/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75fd35db-6b4e-5820-b6ac-925d24a0f117"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115601"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11764/selection/9a150cbc2d87bcc8386575380f239f8892c7ce6d039aeafcd2cfbde4fcd7ae4b" :answer/id #uuid "c7154e5b-7947-57ca-9b13-d5808022fb91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=5x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11764/selection/cfae2665faef57405cd9e920fb7b75a6a83773bf4979e2e23745e22e921205a2" :answer/id #uuid "92ade8a5-6a78-55a7-a78b-53a888a10bed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11764/selection/e2ac2577bc1511d2fb55bb11f333d5433ab3d6a316b25257932f20b05c7c49e3" :answer/id #uuid "836474c3-7627-55a8-b6b0-4935a119fbfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11764/selection/0a8eeb5fd7cf4ecec2547e82e37d28aada07ac627505caa80b41e59c53cbd5e1" :answer/id #uuid "5caf1559-eb72-5ea3-b290-ae00f47abf07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11764/selection/5464b6528434685d90a63424ddd11c4edd590ea7e9ed4845e0656c30ab8dba3b" :answer/id #uuid "34789850-bb68-590a-b76d-e3be9095b691" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11764/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c31a56b-ee2b-53a2-a29d-45fb5b079895" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11764/selection/e2ac2577bc1511d2fb55bb11f333d5433ab3d6a316b25257932f20b05c7c49e3" :answer-field/choices ["q-11764/selection/9a150cbc2d87bcc8386575380f239f8892c7ce6d039aeafcd2cfbde4fcd7ae4b" "q-11764/selection/cfae2665faef57405cd9e920fb7b75a6a83773bf4979e2e23745e22e921205a2" "q-11764/selection/e2ac2577bc1511d2fb55bb11f333d5433ab3d6a316b25257932f20b05c7c49e3" "q-11764/selection/0a8eeb5fd7cf4ecec2547e82e37d28aada07ac627505caa80b41e59c53cbd5e1" "q-11764/selection/5464b6528434685d90a63424ddd11c4edd590ea7e9ed4845e0656c30ab8dba3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11764" :question/id #uuid "065fc101-a0e2-56a3-9672-33a997991742" :question/math-academy-id "q-11764" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/assets/83439b98fff25c021a2713448779167f25a0b9f04dd0d14b115a55f915e3501d.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(12,6).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(12,6),$ we can substitute $x=12$ and $y=6$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {6}^{2} & =4p(12) \\\\ 36 & =48p \\\\ p & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{3}{4})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=\\frac{3}{4}$ is positive." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11764/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75fd35db-6b4e-5820-b6ac-925d24a0f117"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11764"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11750/selection/bee0ef55b953ebc03c79e2074a83df8414202f94b2ac7043220d384e29cc8e9c" :answer/id #uuid "9ffc591d-10ab-59a2-aae6-4cf077e4f94d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=8x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11750/selection/0a8eeb5fd7cf4ecec2547e82e37d28aada07ac627505caa80b41e59c53cbd5e1" :answer/id #uuid "26a0af48-afbe-5a03-bcd1-4c94ec5d4e7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11750/selection/de0b677261bde629b5e156f8561b705314fbfb38516123f6ed9161ad8add8643" :answer/id #uuid "17669a5a-57fe-539c-bffd-87a4fe3b023e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11750/selection/7a51c7b41e0faa12691fd9ae585e993d25d73d9e1ff7e456dc3ad6d9744e0710" :answer/id #uuid "a2eba45d-9fa2-54c1-aa3f-6cf10c2beb51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-8x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11750/selection/6db1b3e26b30525d4ed7a09400dccbe999a5c2e2b1954ea0dec60d75c907de2c" :answer/id #uuid "3cc2b354-e19b-5b69-b8c3-1f46f5f0da8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11750/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba363e23-37f7-59d9-99d5-05731f83c2c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11750/selection/bee0ef55b953ebc03c79e2074a83df8414202f94b2ac7043220d384e29cc8e9c" :answer-field/choices ["q-11750/selection/bee0ef55b953ebc03c79e2074a83df8414202f94b2ac7043220d384e29cc8e9c" "q-11750/selection/0a8eeb5fd7cf4ecec2547e82e37d28aada07ac627505caa80b41e59c53cbd5e1" "q-11750/selection/de0b677261bde629b5e156f8561b705314fbfb38516123f6ed9161ad8add8643" "q-11750/selection/7a51c7b41e0faa12691fd9ae585e993d25d73d9e1ff7e456dc3ad6d9744e0710" "q-11750/selection/6db1b3e26b30525d4ed7a09400dccbe999a5c2e2b1954ea0dec60d75c907de2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11750" :question/id #uuid "9763dfd0-41fb-5dba-b188-a16eaef5f08a" :question/math-academy-id "q-11750" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/assets/b2caf9c9ff75af69d9de7bd1409317229b5d34adf2c64464cd2af2229af0476b.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(8,8).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(8,8),$ we can substitute $x=8$ and $y=8$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {8}^{2} & =4p(8) \\\\ 64 & =32p \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(2)x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =8x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=2$ is positive." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11750/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75fd35db-6b4e-5820-b6ac-925d24a0f117"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11750"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115602/selection/4a0b7ae3b9cd2f9cf9bfb9b6df84cfe39f2b0e766248834edb1822e30d2a3514" :answer/id #uuid "aa402c91-1fa2-5915-b3ee-0acd9fab9b9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=9x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115602/selection/c8d243df1e90dfbf391d6335d56db5f8dd6151b4a8f5316099f703f3742d9cd7" :answer/id #uuid "3a5b98eb-0316-5683-9226-32a216b58c8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115602/selection/8d341c3ca8564f96ecdb6064fae793b79631221f57d2fd0d7e50fbbacc7f7f13" :answer/id #uuid "863278e1-1baf-5375-9be9-5ba04c6ae397" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115602/selection/fb36af8489e2410bf71426275e6327dc6a5e60ff014bcae0672b2a6d3a369bf1" :answer/id #uuid "f34fd5e5-5c04-5e97-becb-4cfa44b4dfad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-9x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115602/selection/fd3e75cf5e1d1eab81b297704f033f2060104ce81b6e79556a5bffd354593760" :answer/id #uuid "4d4123f9-9eee-5ae3-9336-37c9672c6daf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{12}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115602/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a80d8690-cdb4-5371-964c-f34391dd22e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115602/selection/4a0b7ae3b9cd2f9cf9bfb9b6df84cfe39f2b0e766248834edb1822e30d2a3514" :answer-field/choices ["q-115602/selection/4a0b7ae3b9cd2f9cf9bfb9b6df84cfe39f2b0e766248834edb1822e30d2a3514" "q-115602/selection/c8d243df1e90dfbf391d6335d56db5f8dd6151b4a8f5316099f703f3742d9cd7" "q-115602/selection/8d341c3ca8564f96ecdb6064fae793b79631221f57d2fd0d7e50fbbacc7f7f13" "q-115602/selection/fb36af8489e2410bf71426275e6327dc6a5e60ff014bcae0672b2a6d3a369bf1" "q-115602/selection/fd3e75cf5e1d1eab81b297704f033f2060104ce81b6e79556a5bffd354593760"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115602" :question/id #uuid "63dd6ea0-6088-5bea-b162-dd607da9df2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-115602" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/assets/5746a438eccdd55d345f1c71a768f971aa1a342798743e151f7557102ddd8783.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(1,-3).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(1,-3),$ we can substitute $x=1$ and $y=-3$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-3)^{2} & =4p(1) \\\\ 9 & =4p \\\\ p & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{9}{4})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =9x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=\\frac{9}{4}$ is positive." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115602/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75fd35db-6b4e-5820-b6ac-925d24a0f117"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115602"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-11755"] :question/problem "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-12,-4).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-12,-4),$ we can substitute $x=-12$ and $y=-4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-4)^{2} & =4p(-12) \\\\ 16 & =-48p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{3})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{4}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-11753/selection/0a8eeb5fd7cf4ecec2547e82e37d28aada07ac627505caa80b41e59c53cbd5e1" :answer/id #uuid "a2839a73-5fc4-55ed-ae92-7c2c10688e89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11753/selection/bc159fa037ddd299186fbb2d8f6c509131b7677bdd73e951522e3373f16a83a9" :answer/id #uuid "125c3fff-2785-596b-a01a-897e89c7ba49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=6x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11753/selection/de0b677261bde629b5e156f8561b705314fbfb38516123f6ed9161ad8add8643" :answer/id #uuid "adf500d5-2e8f-5c16-802d-888b11c81073" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11753/selection/6db1b3e26b30525d4ed7a09400dccbe999a5c2e2b1954ea0dec60d75c907de2c" :answer/id #uuid "65466d94-7c2c-551a-910d-0e6e936bbaf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11753/selection/cfae2665faef57405cd9e920fb7b75a6a83773bf4979e2e23745e22e921205a2" :answer/id #uuid "9e116112-fc0a-5b35-a911-c4776f11c6a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11753/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7025a21-86cb-5a6d-b7e9-4de911044a5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11753/selection/6db1b3e26b30525d4ed7a09400dccbe999a5c2e2b1954ea0dec60d75c907de2c" :answer-field/choices ["q-11753/selection/0a8eeb5fd7cf4ecec2547e82e37d28aada07ac627505caa80b41e59c53cbd5e1" "q-11753/selection/bc159fa037ddd299186fbb2d8f6c509131b7677bdd73e951522e3373f16a83a9" "q-11753/selection/de0b677261bde629b5e156f8561b705314fbfb38516123f6ed9161ad8add8643" "q-11753/selection/6db1b3e26b30525d4ed7a09400dccbe999a5c2e2b1954ea0dec60d75c907de2c" "q-11753/selection/cfae2665faef57405cd9e920fb7b75a6a83773bf4979e2e23745e22e921205a2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11753" :question/id #uuid "ddce684b-4aee-55f2-8f41-df9cf7650767" :question/math-academy-id "q-11753" :question/problem "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at  $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(8,4).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(8,4),$ we can substitute $x=8$ and $y=4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {4}^{2} & =4p(8) \\\\ 16 & =32p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{2})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11753/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17099881-d7b9-54d9-a29a-4f5f28561cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11753"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115628/selection/e2ac2577bc1511d2fb55bb11f333d5433ab3d6a316b25257932f20b05c7c49e3" :answer/id #uuid "01d233ff-3072-5b18-944b-b02ee8d9abd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115628/selection/9c54f0af3d69efd58d42df4dd2d01b44f8ba1c5e7436c6a99a0acfc037170937" :answer/id #uuid "f62f08c3-9282-52d0-aa58-9736bcc5f891" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{2}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115628/selection/1fddecf590e6991b6c2ecadd87159d86834567662f012a6ba254432b8cf0ddf0" :answer/id #uuid "35208a11-cac5-5ddb-9215-2b2702b86880" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{3}{8}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115628/selection/1a25fa143b052b1bcd8ef371a372cc42309f86bafeec1b9b7e582070454ad508" :answer/id #uuid "98e9cf64-597f-53e7-a207-447b3025e3e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=12y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115628/selection/edfd7f7911c36687a47d4aa87ba77960b2bbe57a19bcf9dc7e97a30d021e291f" :answer/id #uuid "cd1444a6-2b6a-5ff1-86a0-a1285e7f416e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{3}{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115628/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "28e8489d-814a-5a40-bbbe-9db79a6d6349" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115628/selection/edfd7f7911c36687a47d4aa87ba77960b2bbe57a19bcf9dc7e97a30d021e291f" :answer-field/choices ["q-115628/selection/e2ac2577bc1511d2fb55bb11f333d5433ab3d6a316b25257932f20b05c7c49e3" "q-115628/selection/9c54f0af3d69efd58d42df4dd2d01b44f8ba1c5e7436c6a99a0acfc037170937" "q-115628/selection/1fddecf590e6991b6c2ecadd87159d86834567662f012a6ba254432b8cf0ddf0" "q-115628/selection/1a25fa143b052b1bcd8ef371a372cc42309f86bafeec1b9b7e582070454ad508" "q-115628/selection/edfd7f7911c36687a47d4aa87ba77960b2bbe57a19bcf9dc7e97a30d021e291f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115628" :question/id #uuid "a68d4700-937a-5970-9474-6c3ea57e6d2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-115628" :question/problem "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at  $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(6,3).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(6,3),$ we can substitute $x=6$ and $y=3$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {3}^{2} & =4p(6) \\\\ 9 & =24p \\\\ p & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{3}{8})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{2}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115628/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17099881-d7b9-54d9-a29a-4f5f28561cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115628"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11809/selection/f6146f1a2e397c05863f74b05e074a9bf8fccfeeea04a490bdae457b7d63510f" :answer/id #uuid "e0a11b81-08cb-549a-aa0d-ae3e0d3bb564" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=9(x+6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11809/selection/dd4b4c7a7161081c28c49fd7e56976ee478f7b778dc64490247a01b7117ab413" :answer/id #uuid "14ec2148-504f-51d9-bbe2-f2e8b8c8f1a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-6(x+6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11809/selection/df5839ea6a09429d33ba79d45ab67ae392a70f2d84a8b5337bafb64785ca52c0" :answer/id #uuid "736f2b13-f95f-54b4-a35a-3b4ade2bf066" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=6(x+6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11809/selection/32a9f6205923ba5808545420675eab2c038ee7002e56a71c7d1b55d6f3b26a35" :answer/id #uuid "09d6edf5-02f9-5dd8-8c22-42d02acde45d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-9(x+6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11809/selection/8e398d435719d9cb7e3ef84a220f8a91308853fa028f0fd154e2c75a86967f6c" :answer/id #uuid "9b73ddac-f0dd-5a07-8952-bc8df276d9f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+6)^{2}=9x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11809/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aca9e253-d0f4-5fd2-8168-4ff04958883f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11809/selection/f6146f1a2e397c05863f74b05e074a9bf8fccfeeea04a490bdae457b7d63510f" :answer-field/choices ["q-11809/selection/f6146f1a2e397c05863f74b05e074a9bf8fccfeeea04a490bdae457b7d63510f" "q-11809/selection/dd4b4c7a7161081c28c49fd7e56976ee478f7b778dc64490247a01b7117ab413" "q-11809/selection/df5839ea6a09429d33ba79d45ab67ae392a70f2d84a8b5337bafb64785ca52c0" "q-11809/selection/32a9f6205923ba5808545420675eab2c038ee7002e56a71c7d1b55d6f3b26a35" "q-11809/selection/8e398d435719d9cb7e3ef84a220f8a91308853fa028f0fd154e2c75a86967f6c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11809" :question/id #uuid "4f9e3ec6-bada-5b20-a030-4179303dbd69" :question/math-academy-id "q-11809" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/assets/8a48fcacc437d1dca41df82e24984507a92d686f80f4517c6682e8b14b694f0e.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(-6,0)$ and passes through the point $(-2,6).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-6,0),$ we substitute $h=-6$ and $k=0$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4p(x+6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(-2,6),$ so we can substitute $x=-2$ and $y=6$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4p(x+6) \\\\ {6}^{2} & =4p(-2+6) \\\\ 36 & =16p \\\\ p & =\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4p(x+6) \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{9}{4})(x+6) \\\\ {y}^{2} & =9(x+6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=\\frac{9}{4}$ is positive." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11809/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc86c375-c2c4-56b7-a207-0abfc9709f6a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11809"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11799/selection/cc7621e989b9f175b4ff447e51332224c8a6cff37578c738d82616545dec0ea7" :answer/id #uuid "b6e3edf6-247c-5ad0-944d-2113669874b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+4)^{2}=-(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11799/selection/fa80a9789466d68b834bd73710f234589cb204ac156397a828309a39ce403333" :answer/id #uuid "bb7ea5e5-0396-55e0-847f-322d6d7b31fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-4)^{2}=-(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11799/selection/38e57eec5b928faf4c8a25d465485150702d42b7605a636fe132b95dc46146e5" :answer/id #uuid "916f06c8-6b21-5e89-96cf-d49aafb604ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+4)^{2}=(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11799/selection/17595d55e7181e60601b73ef5bfc1212963c0b38eefb9bae0237b84aefc81a7a" :answer/id #uuid "867f9508-85f8-53c3-8602-3ff66b9654ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+4)^{2}=2(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11799/selection/4e3f2d7aa153b18d1a8f914f81683fcf27a1c28445886f33ca2566e2435e1393" :answer/id #uuid "0fbaf54c-3768-5f72-9b2f-3bd068d3f867" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+4)^{2}=-2(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11799/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "70af8dfc-cbcc-5664-a7ec-456b2f89d652" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11799/selection/cc7621e989b9f175b4ff447e51332224c8a6cff37578c738d82616545dec0ea7" :answer-field/choices ["q-11799/selection/cc7621e989b9f175b4ff447e51332224c8a6cff37578c738d82616545dec0ea7" "q-11799/selection/fa80a9789466d68b834bd73710f234589cb204ac156397a828309a39ce403333" "q-11799/selection/38e57eec5b928faf4c8a25d465485150702d42b7605a636fe132b95dc46146e5" "q-11799/selection/17595d55e7181e60601b73ef5bfc1212963c0b38eefb9bae0237b84aefc81a7a" "q-11799/selection/4e3f2d7aa153b18d1a8f914f81683fcf27a1c28445886f33ca2566e2435e1393"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11799" :question/id #uuid "ae27821d-0ab5-56dd-86d2-1c08394a25d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-11799" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/assets/872c4385f2f7075ac4f9690f5adabaa8cb6b4ad3ffe738b47f2b22e477aab621.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(4,-4)$ and passes through the point $(0,-6).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(4,-4),$ we substitute $h=4$ and $k=-4$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+4)^{2} & =4p(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(0,-6),$ so we can substitute $x=0$ and $y=-6$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+4)^{2} & =4p(x-4) \\\\ (-6+4)^{2} & =4p(0-4) \\\\ 4 & =-16p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+4)^{2} & =4p(x-4) \\\\ (y+4)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{4})(x-4) \\\\ (y+4)^{2} & =-(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the left since $p=-\\frac{1}{4}$ is negative." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11799/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc86c375-c2c4-56b7-a207-0abfc9709f6a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11799"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-11807"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/assets/e4b681e9bdf5fa8021ca359e0bf93c27b53a18f0d5e906765a911a72ecfc0159.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-11803/selection/d81b73438159290996f1ead751eb03a4a8b5faf1f164bb07b1a145c1a80ee132" :answer/id #uuid "46ee4426-8b1d-5151-98d6-689fe9d9ede1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=4(x-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11803/selection/74d80839843713d21b1cc12c95050411e36eefd0808e5ed59df97ea63ef11649" :answer/id #uuid "1f2f213e-c066-5328-ad5d-a8fb164f7b85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+2)^{2}=-6(x+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11803/selection/f82da756f05366ca431bd0682b796269863760fa46670a34c71944d32a4ca0dd" :answer/id #uuid "30328629-2e13-58c6-b050-dc64685ae511" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=-4(x-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11803/selection/3cc1e04f9fc27f131b3fff54c172812446207d5c1e88d21e29c9fdb4bd3127c1" :answer/id #uuid "11bd0983-2bce-59a1-9270-c538c84dc453" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=6(x-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11803/selection/5c61c4afcc8d8ebe814be3895d688a1dd284b9d0d74e7333453c17cadf973c3a" :answer/id #uuid "a1f2796e-58be-5a9b-96f8-870b9a333ab0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=-6(x-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11803/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ae327a2-5e21-5cce-a8ae-dd3c52c53403" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11803/selection/5c61c4afcc8d8ebe814be3895d688a1dd284b9d0d74e7333453c17cadf973c3a" :answer-field/choices ["q-11803/selection/d81b73438159290996f1ead751eb03a4a8b5faf1f164bb07b1a145c1a80ee132" "q-11803/selection/74d80839843713d21b1cc12c95050411e36eefd0808e5ed59df97ea63ef11649" "q-11803/selection/f82da756f05366ca431bd0682b796269863760fa46670a34c71944d32a4ca0dd" "q-11803/selection/3cc1e04f9fc27f131b3fff54c172812446207d5c1e88d21e29c9fdb4bd3127c1" "q-11803/selection/5c61c4afcc8d8ebe814be3895d688a1dd284b9d0d74e7333453c17cadf973c3a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11803" :question/id #uuid "eba2b56d-84e3-51b1-8610-87cab958ffe0" :question/math-academy-id "q-11803" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/assets/814515b0294849e2689214faa1ac97a4f0bb5134f3209a9fb0b2fdbda5c2a484.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(2,2)$ and passes through the point $(-4,8).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(2,2),$ we substitute $h=2$ and $k=2$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(-4,8),$ so we can substitute $x=-4$ and $y=8$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x-2) \\\\ (8-2)^{2} & =4p(-4-2) \\\\ 36 & =-24p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x-2) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{3}{2})(x-2) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =-6(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the left since $p=-\\frac{3}{2}$ is negative." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11803/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc86c375-c2c4-56b7-a207-0abfc9709f6a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11803"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-115640"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/assets/c88e54f2a7acec3815a53fa4b0d641dd370ccf708b876f8dd231f05e115ea6fc.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-11796"] :question/problem "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(-1,1)$ and passes through the point $(8,7).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-1,1),$ we substitute $h=-1$ and $k=1$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-1)^{2} & =4p(x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(8,7),$ so we can substitute $x=8$ and $y=7$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-1)^{2} & =4p(x+1) \\\\ (7-1)^{2} & =4p(8+1) \\\\ 36 & =36p \\\\ p & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-1)^{2} & =4p(x+1) \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =4(1)(x+1) \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =4(x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-11802/selection/05337557b4ab4facb94c73a46d1367a06f9c91f40a5341a63ae5c8e2502e73c6" :answer/id #uuid "68772979-cfd4-56e8-aa50-0a73282be9f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}(x-5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11802/selection/f5d962f22a5749e98b080c603b7251d196ba5a209374526e5d2ee2f62aef0294" :answer/id #uuid "1cc21b2b-9aa9-5713-8a64-935acb5ccd08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=-\\frac{4}{3}(x-5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11802/selection/192def2c61965fb23adecf31599635bac132c545e28832897ab11483a04bed7b" :answer/id #uuid "4a40c676-cc13-587b-a046-2be557ce51d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}(x-5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11802/selection/5d7a1de710ecbe3dec2eafe66cfba4af4cda7af69e5918ecf465078cc0027682" :answer/id #uuid "c9093ec0-2056-5f09-86a8-b82e6aea7486" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}(x-5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11802/selection/35c035031b7bccf1b2014e9bf2d70ac0c91d9a8d27834d05540b739affeea9cf" :answer/id #uuid "1b86afe4-c17d-5595-b4ba-b3a1a292227d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-5)^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11802/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "03e1b577-4090-53d3-83b8-be0f8ae6c08f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11802/selection/192def2c61965fb23adecf31599635bac132c545e28832897ab11483a04bed7b" :answer-field/choices ["q-11802/selection/05337557b4ab4facb94c73a46d1367a06f9c91f40a5341a63ae5c8e2502e73c6" "q-11802/selection/f5d962f22a5749e98b080c603b7251d196ba5a209374526e5d2ee2f62aef0294" "q-11802/selection/192def2c61965fb23adecf31599635bac132c545e28832897ab11483a04bed7b" "q-11802/selection/5d7a1de710ecbe3dec2eafe66cfba4af4cda7af69e5918ecf465078cc0027682" "q-11802/selection/35c035031b7bccf1b2014e9bf2d70ac0c91d9a8d27834d05540b739affeea9cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11802" :question/id #uuid "eca8fc36-230f-507e-b2dc-9fc7682f36b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-11802" :question/problem "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(5,1)$ and passes through the point $(-1,5).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(5,1),$ we substitute $h=5$ and $k=1$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-1)^{2} & =4p(x-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(-1,5),$ so we can substitute $x=-1$ and $y=5$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-1)^{2} & =4p(x-5) \\\\ (5-1)^{2} & =4p(-1-5) \\\\ 16 & =-24p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-1)^{2} & =4p(x-5) \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{2}{3})(x-5) \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =-\\frac{8}{3}(x-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11802/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "783ca59b-0242-584c-ae47-004a0eb03817"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11802"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11812/selection/f0992ec756af5d42ea30786716313d38fec14dc448628f32f696fb0d1d3cfcc0" :answer/id #uuid "1c47fd6d-6cdf-56a6-a81d-acf0ea7c9d63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=-2(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11812/selection/7bd49de06c7d526aeed4c7c0eef991385eb7d56e64512ff29f23c9b90ced96cd" :answer/id #uuid "9ea89fb8-18ff-5c75-b6e9-250f1413743e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=2(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11812/selection/0afbb80cb6196d1d0dd4289b5ae618c968283403a6dbc664413baf01d8178e49" :answer/id #uuid "d26db3da-3c62-5054-8e8e-e5a6a99300e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=5(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11812/selection/6a2f023e198fcb05a0544659259d48322630ba0f19d3cb16a88e367821f3ca74" :answer/id #uuid "d93a2c22-0665-5154-9291-21aea4d1aa04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=-5(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11812/selection/cfd483f3860ae9247226748a023ad5c04e2547861070e6d7c1c38789e304db00" :answer/id #uuid "d3d0bc6c-1fbd-553a-9172-f9a2feca6e07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+4)^{2}=5(x+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11812/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4916f60e-9b36-5255-b31f-77287070bcbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11812/selection/0afbb80cb6196d1d0dd4289b5ae618c968283403a6dbc664413baf01d8178e49" :answer-field/choices ["q-11812/selection/f0992ec756af5d42ea30786716313d38fec14dc448628f32f696fb0d1d3cfcc0" "q-11812/selection/7bd49de06c7d526aeed4c7c0eef991385eb7d56e64512ff29f23c9b90ced96cd" "q-11812/selection/0afbb80cb6196d1d0dd4289b5ae618c968283403a6dbc664413baf01d8178e49" "q-11812/selection/6a2f023e198fcb05a0544659259d48322630ba0f19d3cb16a88e367821f3ca74" "q-11812/selection/cfd483f3860ae9247226748a023ad5c04e2547861070e6d7c1c38789e304db00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11812" :question/id #uuid "0644416e-9146-5c0c-b6e4-b37a6a1d8844" :question/math-academy-id "q-11812" :question/problem "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(-4,-3)$ and passes through the point $(1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-4,-3),$ we substitute $h=-4$ and $k=-3$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(1,2),$ so we can substitute $x=1$ and $y=2$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x+4) \\\\ (2+3)^{2} & =4p(1+4) \\\\ 25 & =20p \\\\ p & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x+4) \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =4(\\frac{5}{4})(x+4) \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =5(x+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11812/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "783ca59b-0242-584c-ae47-004a0eb03817"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11812"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5333"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/assets/70ff1c84aa4a9a2adc393fc1dcf684ee0bcf161671b15f9061e2319f5d7e0a39.png)\n\n  \n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-8,4).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\ny^2  = 4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-8,4),$ we can substitute $x = -8$ and $y = 4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {4}^{2} & =4p(-8) \\\\ 16 & =-32p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{2})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the left since $p = -\\dfrac{1}{2}$ is negative." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5334"] :question/problem "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(4,4).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\ny^2  = 4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(4,4),$ we can substitute $x=4$ and $y=4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {4}^{2} & =4p(4) \\\\ 16 & =16p \\\\ p & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(1)x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5335"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/assets/55651f756b31405e08cd96b097101528ffabff1e6411d3fcae9f40f747f607b4.png)\n\n  \n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(4,2)$ and passes through the point $(0,6).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h, k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h, k) = (4,2),$ we substitute $h=4$ and $k=2$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(0,6),$ so we can substitute $x=0$ and $y=6$ into the equation above and solve for $p\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x-4) \\\\ (6-2)^{2} & =4p(0-4) \\\\ 16 & =-16p \\\\ p & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x-4) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4(-1)(x-4) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =-4(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the left since $p = -1$ is negative." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5336"] :question/problem "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(2,-2)$ and passes through the point $(-6,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h, k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h, k) = (2,-2),$ we substitute $h=2$ and $k=-2$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+2)^{2} & =4p(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(-6, 2),$ so we can substitute $x=-6$ and $y=2$ into the equation above and solve for $p\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+2)^{2} & =4p(x-2) \\\\ (2+2)^{2} & =4p(-6-2) \\\\ 16 & =-32p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+2)^{2} & =4p(x-2) \\\\ (y+2)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{2})(x-2) \\\\ (y+2)^{2} & =-2(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
